ven if you  buy a cheaper house even if you say well  I'm going to find a house for a hundred  and fifty thousand pounds all right fine  you're still going to need half of 90.  still gonna need 45  000 pounds and with 45 000 pounds you're  only going to end up owning one house  I'm going to show you how you can get 10  nice houses so that  sucks that's old school that's what  losers do that's what people do that  don't understand the formulas that is  not how any rich people invest in  property this is how wealthy people  invest these are the formulas so you're  going to find a house  okay and you're going to go to an area  whereby you're going to do market  research on the street look at all the  houses in the street and see how much  they're selling for let's say the  average house in that street is selling  for 200 000 pounds which is very doable  200 000 pounds you're gonna find  I don't want that house I don't want  that house you're gonna find the houses  which are in really bad condition  they're really run down  now the great thing about finding houses  that are run down let's say it's got  structural problems the roof needs  fixing there's no kitchen no bathroom no  installation it's a wreck the great  thing about that is  firstly you can buy it really cheap it  might need let's say 50 000 pounds  spending on it but but secondly not only  can you buy cheap below market value but  no one else can buy that house and the  reason no one can buy that house that's  run down is because there's no mortgage  lender that will loan money on a house  that's in really bad condition they  won't do it you can't get a Residential  Mortgage you can't get a buyer because  you're not buying it to let it it's run  down you can't get any type of mortgage  so what that means is houses like this  that may be our probate Properties or  they're being they've been repossessed  and now they've been sold off cheap by  the Banks houses like this which exist  all over the place that are run down  they first-time buyers biceps landlords  can't buy it but the only people that  can buy these types of houses are cash  buyers so you can buy them cheap so  let's say you agreed to buy a house like  this it's really run down it's 50 000  pounds spending on it and you agree to  buy it for a hundred thousand pounds  which again is realistic it is 50  Instagram spending on it it is elbow  grease it needs three to six months  worth of work so what you do is here's  how you financially structure it you  can't get a mortgage on it you can't you  can't buy it cash because you've only  got 50 000 pounds so you're gonna get  something called a bridge  now a bridge is something that Bridges  the gap between you purchasing the house  and you then later getting a mortgage  because you can only get a mortgage or a  refinance on the house when it's in good  condition when it's mortgageable so you  buy it for 100 grand how much are  bridging companies going to loan you  well I know because I actually have my  own bridging Finance Company they're  going to typically loan you about 65  percent  of the purchase price and they will loan  you the money for the refurb so they're  going to give you 65 Grand that means  that you only need 35 Grand  okay plus your legal fees and stuff  maybe an extra 5 000 pounds Max so 40  000 pounds  to buy the house because you're going to  get a bridging loan that will pay the  rest you're going to get a bridging loan  that will pay the purchase a bridge and  loan company that will pay the the 50  000 pounds now of course you're gonna  have to pay the bridging loan company to  do this typically you're going to pay  one percent a month so if you've got the  money for six months let's say by the  way you're gonna pay zero stamp Duty on  this property because it's inhabitable  that's another little trick so let's say  you end up in tow with all your legal  fees and everything spending 50 000  pounds  which is the amount that I've said in  this 